I’m using a single explicit loop so the proof can attach one circularity directly to the program’s loop head. The loop maintains a growing output prefix; at index `i`, that prefix equals the first `i` positions of the original list with every third position drawn, in order, from the trusted `sorted(l[::3])` sequence. This gives an unbounded structural theorem over a symbolic `ValSeq`, while the fixed semantics still executes the actual function body, calls, indexing, branches, and heap updates.
