codex
The first genuine residual is at builtin lookup, not at the invariant algebra: the loop claim left the function’s parent scope abstract, so the prover correctly could not establish that `len` resolves to the builtin. I’m tightening the invariant to the actual call-frame chain (`callee → module → builtins`) while still leaving the module’s unrelated bindings symbolic; this preserves binding fidelity rather than bypassing lookup.
apply patch
